    summary: `Deep learning training fails in many ways, most of them silent or misleading. Loss spikes, NaN gradients, mode collapse in generative models, and unexpected plateaus each have distinct root causes that require systematic debugging. The debugging mindset is scientific: isolate, hypothesise, verify. The two most diagnostic tests are "overfit one batch" (verifies the model can learn anything) and "check gradient flow" (verifies gradients reach early layers). Senior ML engineers spend more time on debugging workflow than architecture novelty — the skill gap between junior and senior is primarily here. Every training failure has a unique fingerprint in the loss curve, gradient norms, and activation statistics that experienced engineers learn to read quickly.`,
